MODEL_FEEDBACK_JSON:
{
  "positive_alignment_reasons": [
    "The rotary burrs, metric bolts and rubber grommets fit connected steps in my projects: drilling and deburring panels, fastening parts and protecting wires through holes.",
    "The thermal camera and clamp meter felt useful for home troubleshooting. They extend the inspection work suggested by my borescope and infrared thermometer purchases."
  ],
  "negative_misalignment_reasons": [
    "The glass lifters and tension straps require jobs I have not shown a need for. Doing fabrication does not mean I currently need to lift glass or secure loads.",
    "The EMF and decibel meters offer measurements without a clear problem I need to solve. My interest in inspection tools depends on what they help me diagnose."
  ],
  "overgeneralized_signals": [
    "Owning several workshop tools seemed to count too heavily as a reason to suggest equipment for unrelated workshop tasks.",
    "My measurement-tool purchases seemed to imply interest in any kind of meter, although I choose tools for specific repair questions."
  ],
  "missing_or_underweighted_signals": [
    "Compatibility matters before I choose an accessory: the recommended wheels are 4.5 inches while my recent wheels were 5 inches, and I would need to check the burrs' shank fit.",
    "My repeated hardware purchases make complementary sizes, head styles and uses relevant. The metric hex head bolts could add something useful alongside my existing socket head and stainless assortments."
  ],
  "summary_diagnosis": "The recommendations understood my fastening, fabrication and repair interests, but sometimes stretched them into tools without a clear job in my current work."
}
